A||||13||danny boy||4cyl 5sp in V6 car||||5||
Z||000000||danny boy||01-29-2001||07:48 PM|||| I know this has probably been discussed before but...<BR> Has anyone ever put a 5speed out of a 4cyl car into a V6 car and had sucess? I know it bolts right in basically,but will it hold up?<BR>Ive heard that it will break but if archie says they'll hold V8 power why not a V6? The car in question is pretty much stock.oh, and how do you post pics on here? I'm not real good with these computer thingys.||||reg||5
Z||000001||ray b||01-29-2001||10:47 PM||||has been done how long it will last is open question some say good some dont last. depends on your driving style and luck. ray||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||01-30-2001||01:08 AM||||I've never heard of one failing, in either a V8 or a V6.  Any transmission can and will fail if it's abused.  If you have any plans of racing your car I'd stay away from it, but otherwise you should be fine if you drive sane  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Just so ya' know, it's the Isuzu transmission with an RPO code of MT2.  I've heard that the ratios fit the V6 pretty good, but I think I'll stick to my Getrag  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||
Z||000003||Elenor84||01-30-2001||03:45 AM||||Ok, now u just said that if u plan on racing don't put that transmissioin in...but why do people put v8's in there cars?  To drive as slow as possible?  Hell no...to burn rubber and go faster...so why should he stay away from it if it will hold up?<BR>thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sideview.jpg">  </A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||TheFiero64||01-30-2001||11:37 AM||||I have the izuzu 5 speed in my 88 V6. I love the Isuzu 5sp. I think it shifts smoother than the Getrag. There are a bunch of us v6 w/Isuzu 5's. I have 160,000 on my Isuzu and I drive it hard. It still runs like new.<P>Look at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001206-2-002635.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001206-2-002635.html</A> ||||reg||4
Z||000005||Standard||01-30-2001||02:41 PM||||Just because you put a V8 in doesn't mean you are going to abuse the tranny.  If the V8 guys did drop-clutch starts and speed shifts, they'd be blowing tranny's left and right.  Tina's 383 snapped her 4-spd pretty much in half...  what I'm trying to say is that it will have a much shorter life if it's abused.  You might get lucky and it'll last forever doing smokey burnouts, or it could break when you're putting down the street.<P>Actually, I have heard of one isuzu meltdown behind a v6, on the highway.  I think it's somewhere on the Fiero Online Service Guide.<p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 01-30-2001).]||||reg||
Z||000006||Elenor84||01-31-2001||05:52 AM||||Why would u do clutch dropping in a v8?  u can pull blackies in 2nd gear in a 350...u don't need to abuse the clutch to make a v8 go...<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sideview.jpg">  </A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bill 88||01-31-2001||03:00 PM||||What do you want for the v-6 wiring harness?  I might be interested.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Standard||01-31-2001||05:38 PM||||I'm not talking about abusing the clutch, I'm talking about abusing the tranny.  Snapping tranny cases, gears, etc...  There always has to be a weak link.  Now, ideally, you want that to be the tires, have them break traction before breaking the tranny.  But alot of people who put v8's in also put some pretty wide tires in the back so they can get traction in the first place.  That can transfer the weak link to a different spot.. clutch, tranny, axles, crankshaft...  what happens when the car pulling a "blackie in 2nd gear" all of the sudden grabs traction, and you still have the pedal to the floor?  If you're lucky, you'll just shoot forward.  If not... <I>snap</I>, or it could just snap while you're doing the burnout... check out the thread from Tina's blown up 4-spd.   <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005209.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005209.html</A> <P>I'm not saying it <B>will</B> break, I'm just saying there's a much higher chance of it.||||reg||
Z||000009||Elenor84||02-01-2001||01:35 AM||||Ok...I understand...so now what I would like to know is...lets say u do a v8 swap...u should replace the clutch and transmistion with a v8 transmission?  Would that solve the problem?  Even if it wasen't a v8 trany...should u just get a new one instead of the 17 year old one that is stock?<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sideview.jpg">  </A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Standard||02-01-2001||01:06 PM||||For the ultimate reliability, yes.  The problem there is that there really is no suitable FWD tranny that you can swap in.  If you can find one, it would probably at least double the cost of the swap.  If you mount the engine longitudinally(north-south) it opens up your options a little, but then you lose your trunk and put a bunch more weight in back.  Either way it would still probably be cheaper/easier to keep a few spare isuzu or muncie tranny's on hand..||||reg||
Z||000011||ChadMan||02-01-2001||01:25 PM||||Is there a heavy-duty clutch available for the Isuzu?  With the extra HP/torque of the V6, I would worry more about the durability of the clutch than the durability of the Isuzu gearbox.||||reg||4
Z||000012||TheFiero64||02-01-2001||03:57 PM||||I think the Fiero store sells a Ram Heavy duty clutch||||reg||1
Z||000013||LarryB||02-01-2001||05:57 PM||||What the Fiero Store refers to as the Heavy Duty clutch Ram calls their OEM clutch set.<P>Looks like you can maybe get a Kevlar composite though: <BR> <A HREF="http://www.ramclutches.com/applications/pontiac%201.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ramclutches.com/applications/pontiac%201.htm</A> <BR>||||reg||1
